# Normalize line endings to LF for every text file, regardless of which
# git client (Windows, WSL/Linux, CI) checks it out or commits it — this
# repo is worked on from both a Windows Git Bash session and native WSL
# Ubuntu git on the same checkout, and without this file the two disagree
# on CRLF vs LF, causing permanent "modified" noise and, once, actual
# local object-store corruption from a bad commit. LF is also simply
# correct here: this is a backend-only project (Deno/TS, SQL, shell,
# JSON), nothing in it has any reason to want CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
